  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3e4b5683c1ea36345958694d590b6436, type: 3}
  m_Name: COC3_Quiz_LO3_Testing_Q01
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuizQuestionData
  questionText: Why is every test in the plan performed on the CLIENT rather than
    on the server?
  choices:
  - The server cannot run the test tools
  - Client hardware is faster for testing
  - A service checked only on the server has not been tested as a user would use
    it
  - Testing on a server can corrupt the configuration
  correctChoiceIndex: 2
  points: 10
  explanation: The server can reach its own folder whatever the share and permissions
    say. Only the client exercises the network, the name resolution, the share and
    the permissions together.
